      "writtenOn": "2026-07-28T21:50:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In fact, it  currently gives 404 by L84 by checking `(ec \u003d\u003d boost::system::errc::io_error)`.\nNote that\n   // getAssociatedSubTreePathsById() returns io_error if processorId does\n   // not exist\n \nHowever, thinking again, it would make more sense to give the empty collection because the parent Processor GET has a link to SubProcessors collection.\n\nredfish-core/lib/processor.hpp:L906 like\n\n```\n  \"SubProcessors\": {\n    \"@odata.id\": \"/redfish/v1/Systems/system/Processors/cpu0/SubProcessors\"\n  },\n```\n\nIf we check the existence and give 404, this parent Processors would also need to check so that it won\u0027t give the link.\n\nSo, I think - it is proper to give the empty collection if it does not exist.\n```\nL81:\n     if (ec \u0026\u0026 ec !\u003d boost::system::errc::io_error)\n      {\n         // getAssociatedSubTreePathsById() returns io_error if processorId does\n        // not exist. Otherwise, it would be dbus error.\n        BMCWEB_LOG_ERROR();\n        messages::internalError();\n        return;\n    }\n```\n\nWhat do you think?",
      "parentUuid": "66be6b99_403d9c21",
